        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Roni Stoneman, Gordie Tapp\n- Roles: Ida Lee Nagger, Laverne Nagger\n- Organizations: Hee Haw, CBS\n- Topics: bluegrass, television, comedy, broadcasting\n\nFacts:\n- Gordie Tapp was born in London, Ontario, on June 4, 1922.\n- Roni Stoneman was born on May 5, 1938.\n- Roni Stoneman is a noted bluegrass banjo player.\n- Roni Stoneman was a former member of the television variety show Hee Haw.\n- On Hee Haw, Roni Stoneman played Ida Lee Nagger, the ironing and nagging wife of Laverne Nagger.\n- Gordie Tapp played Laverne Nagger on Hee Haw.\n- Gordie Tapp was a Canadian entertainer best known as a radio and television presenter, comedian, and CBS broadcaster.\n- Gordie Tapp died on December 18, 2016.",
